	A character of mine became TRULY undead.  It started out innocent
	enough: I was a baby Green Dragon, frozen by a floating eye and
	masticated slowly by a grid bug.  Rather than wear out my space 
	key, I decided to Ctrl-c out and roll up another polymorph ring 
	toting mage.
	
	Do you really wish to quit (y/n)?
	
	"Aw, what the hack, no." sayeth I, remembering this character 
	also had a Pick-axe of Endless Hitpoints.

	The game froze.  Not a creature was stirring, not even a rabbid
	rat.

	Cursing, I opened up another window and killed the process.  Surprise,
	surprise.  When I came back, I was unstuckified!

	So, emulating an HP I wondered what if...  Say I read a scroll of 
	fire, but don't want my 15 potions of holy water transmogrified into
	a blessed steam cloud.  Say I've hit <shift>H on the stronghold
	level and screamed in horror as my character blithely dove head-first
	into the moat, wish wand and all.  (NEW ITEM ALERT: life jacket.)
	Say I wire a Control-C toggle switch to my keyboard...

	Later same game I was being literally eaten alive by a soldier ant.
	Knowing full well that with 2 hit points the very next thing after
	the "the soldier ant stings --more--" would be the graveyard, I 
	merrily sent nethack a "SIGKILL, love Mom."

	Second shocker of the day.  I had NEGATIVE HIT POINTS!  Better yet,
	none of the monsters I met were attacking!  Unfortunately, I died
	anyway "from huger and exhaustion" when eating the corpse.  The
	kicker was that I WASN'T EVEN HUNGRY.  Dead on my feet, maybe.  But
	definitely not hungry.

	And speaking of death by gastrointestinal distress...  In a different
	game, one that I was likely to win, my character was stumbling about 
	the dungeon groaning "I can't believe I ate the WHOLE thing," while 
	picking orange dragon particles out of his teeth.  Lo and behold, a 
	helpless quivering blob looked up at me with big, sad eyes as it 
	innocently tried to crossed the hallway, undoubtedly on its way home 
	to its wife and kids.  With the often heard battle cry of "FOOD!" I 
	murdered it in cold blood (ichor?) and settled down for a fountainside 
	feast.

	The game was not amused by this awesome display of gluttony.  Not
	even a "continue pigging out [y/n]" graced my screen.  Surprisingly
	enough, the scoreboard displays "killed by a quivering blob corpse"
	as the postmortem, not a snide comment about my exuberant appetite.

	What this game needs is a potion of Pepto, or an amulet of continuous
	colonics.

